{
  "dom_id": "step-q251772",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "A stone is projected vertically downward from a height of $29.4\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $17.64\\,\\text{km/h}.$ How long will it take for the stone to hit the ground?\n\n*Hint: The acceleration due to gravity is $9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$*\n\nThe stone hits the ground in{{field-1}}seconds.",
  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we use the formula\n\n$$\ns=ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the displacement, measured from the starting position in the direction of the initial motion, $u$ is the initial velocity, $t$ is the time since the beginning of the motion, and $g$ is the acceleration due to gravity.\n\nLet's summarize the information we have:\n\n- We can find the initial velocity of the stone in meters per second as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =17.64\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{h}} \\\\  & =17.64\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{h}}\\cdot \\frac{1000\\,\\text{m}}{\\text{km}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{h}}{60\\,\\text{min}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{min}}{60\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =17.64\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{km}}}{\\cancel{\\text{h}}}\\cdot \\frac{1000\\,\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{km}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{h}}}{60\\,\\cancel{\\text{min}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{min}}}{60\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =17.64\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{{60}^{2}\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =4.9\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The stone covers the distance of $s=29.4\\,\\text{m}.$\n\n- The acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula and solving for $t,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(29.4) & =(4.9)t+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (9.8){t}^{2} \\\\ 29.4 & =4.9t+4.9{t}^{2} \\\\ 6(4.9) & =(4.9)t+4.9{t}^{2} \\\\ 6\\cancel{(4.9)} & =\\cancel{(4.9)}t+\\cancel{(4.9)}{t}^{2} \\\\ 6 & =t+{t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}+t-6 & =0 \\\\ (t+3)(t-2) & =0 \\\\ t & =-3,\\,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution. Therefore, the stone hits the ground after $t=2$ seconds.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
